{"call_id": "1ff41b1cf3394f4c9d01be00d0dab6c2", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/fullbench/runs/natural/PANCANCER_ATLAS/query3/full-01/results/1ff41b1cf3394f4c9d01be00d0dab6c2.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"stdout\": \"Distinct CDH1 PASS-mutated participants (all cancers): 247\\nFemale BRCA patients with known histological type: 1074\\n\\nAll categories (female BRCA, known histology):\\n  Infiltrating Ductal Carcinoma: mutated=9, not_mutated=757, total=766\\n  Infiltrating Lobular Carcinoma: mutated=83, not_mutated=118, total=201\\n  Other  specify: mutated=3, not_mutated=42, total=45\\n  Mixed Histology (please specify): mutated=4, not_mutated=26, total=30\\n  Mucinous Carcinoma: mutated=0, not_mutated=17, total=17\\n  Metaplastic Carcinoma: mutated=0, not_mutated=8, total=8\\n  Medullary Carcinoma: mutated=1, not_mutated=5, total=6\\n  Infiltrating Carcinoma NOS: mutated=0, not_mutated=1, total=1\\n\\nKept categories (marginal total > 10):\\n  Infiltrating Ductal Carcinoma: mutated=9, not_mutated=757, total=766\\n  Infiltrating Lobular Carcinoma: mutated=83, not_mutated=118, total=201\\n  Other  specify: mutated=3, not_mutated=42, total=45\\n  Mixed Histology (please specify): mutated=4, not_mutated=26, total=30\\n  Mucinous Carcinoma: mutated=0, not_mutated=17, total=17\\n\\nN patients in test: 1059\\nChi-square statistic: 305.1239\\nDegrees of freedom: 4\\np-value: 8.501e-65\\n\", \"stderr\": \"\", \"returncode\": 0}", "truncated": false}
{"call_id": "7514a1518a1e4fbfa05f8ece3a1c67a5", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/fullbench/runs/natural/PANCANCER_ATLAS/query3/full-01/results/7514a1518a1e4fbfa05f8ece3a1c67a5.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"submitted\": true, \"answer\": \"CHI-SQUARE TEST: Histological Type vs. CDH1 Mutation Status in Female BRCA (PanCancer Atlas)\\n\\nMETHOD\\n- Cohort: 1,075 female BRCA (Breast invasive carcinoma) patients identified from the clinical database\\n  (barcode = 'TCGA-' + tissue_source_site + '-' + patient_id; gender extracted from Patient_description).\\n- Restricted to patients with known histological types: 1,074 patients (1 null excluded).\\n- CDH1 mutation presence: patients with at least one reliable CDH1 mutation entry\\n  (Hugo_Symbol = 'CDH1' AND FILTER = 'PASS') in Mutation_Data (247 distinct participants across all cancers;\\n  99 overlapped the female BRCA cohort).\\n- Histological categories with marginal totals <= 10 excluded:\\n  Metaplastic Carcinoma (8), Medullary Carcinoma (6), Infiltrating Carcinoma NOS (1).\\n\\nCONTINGENCY TABLE (N = 1,059; mutated / not mutated)\\n- Infiltrating Ductal Carcinoma:    9  / 757  (total 766)\\n- Infiltrating Lobular Carcinoma:  83  / 118  (total 201)\\n- Other, specify:                   3  / 42   (total 45)\\n- Mixed Histology (please specify): 4  / 26   (total 30)\\n- Mucinous Carcinoma:               0  / 17   (total 17)\\n\\nRESULT\\n- Chi-square statistic: 305.12\\n- Degrees of freedom: 4\\n- p-value: ~8.5e-65\\n\\nINTERPRETATION\\nThere is a highly significant association between histological type and CDH1 mutation status in female\\nBRCA patients. CDH1 mutations are strongly enriched in Infiltrating Lobular Carcinoma (83/201, ~41.3%)\\ncompared with Infiltrating Ductal Carcinoma (9/766, ~1.2%) and other histologies — consistent with the\\nknown biology of lobular breast cancer, which is characterized by CDH1 (E-cadherin) loss.\\n\"}", "truncated": false}
